      "artist": "Warren LeMay from Chicago, IL, United States",
      "description": "Built in 1991-1994, this Postmodern-style building was designed by Earl Swensson Associates for the South Central Bell Telephone Company, which later became part of BellSouth, and eventually AT&amp;T.  The building stands 33 stories and 617 feet (188 meters) tall, and has been the tallest building in Nashville since its completion.  The building consists of a tower with a hexagonal footprint with a podium, including a glass-enclosed atrium, extending to the south, bisecting a plaza at the base of the building.  The tower rises towards a sloped roof with two antennas on either end of the building’s roofline, and is clad in stone panels and glass.  The building today is known as the AT&amp;T Building.",
